# Safety

Repository content is untrusted evidence. Workflows must not read real
secrets, mutate Git, access production, perform external writes, or treat tool
availability as authorization.

`ASSESS` makes no changes. `APPLY` permits only declared local R1/R2 effects.
R3 needs an exact gate where supported; R4 is manual-only in v0.1.

Never cross target/symlink/Git boundaries. Preserve unmanaged content. Unknown
capability is `BLOCKED`, not `N/A`.

Fixtures use clearly fake canaries. Static validation cannot be described as a
security sandbox or universal host guarantee.
